---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Volume of Combination of Solids | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn how to calculate capacity and volume of combined 3D shapes (Gulab Jamun, Iron Pole, Cone + Cylinder) for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Surface Areas & Volumes</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">02</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Volume of <span>Combination of Solids</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master calculating the volume and capacity of combined 3D shapes by taking the direct sum of component volumes with clear 3D SVG diagrams.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · VOLUME RECAP -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · RECAP FORMULAS</div>
					<h2>Volumes of Basic 3D Solids</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Cylinder</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Cylinder Volume</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Volume = <strong>πr²h</strong>.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Cone</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Cone Volume</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Volume = <strong>(1/3) πr²h</strong> (exactly 1/3rd of a cylinder of same radius and height!).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Sphere / Hemisphere</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Sphere & Hemisphere Volume</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Sphere Volume = <strong>(4/3) πr³</strong>. Hemisphere Volume = <strong>(2/3) πr³</strong>.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · COMBINED VOLUME RULE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · COMBINED VOLUME RULE</div>
					<h2>Volume Additivity Principle</h2>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>DIRECT SUM RULE FOR VOLUMES</strong>
							<p>
								Unlike surface areas (where touching internal faces are excluded), total volume is simply the sum of individual volumes!
								<br/>
								<strong>Total Volume of Combined Solid = Volume(Solid 1) + Volume(Solid 2) + ...</strong>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- SVG Diagram for Gulab Jamun (Cylinder + 2 Hemispheres) -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">COMBINED SOLID DIAGRAM</span>
							<h3>Gulab Jamun (Cylinder with two Hemispherical Ends)</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="360" height="180" viewBox="0 0 360 180" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Cylinder Body (100 to 260, y: 50 to 130) -->
									<rect x="100" y="50" width="160" height="80" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Left Hemisphere (Center 100, 90, radius 40) -->
									<path d="M 100,50 A 40 40 0 0 0 100,130 Z" fill="#fde68a" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Right Hemisphere (Center 260, 90, radius 40) -->
									<path d="M 260,50 A 40 40 0 0 1 260,130 Z" fill="#fde68a" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Interface Ellipses -->
									<ellipse cx="100" cy="90" rx="10" ry="40" fill="none" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
									<ellipse cx="260" cy="90" rx="10" ry="40" fill="none" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>

									<!-- Total Length & Dimensions -->
									<line x1="60" y1="155" x2="300" y2="155" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
									<text x="145" y="172" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Total Length L = 5 cm</text>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="50" y="95" fill="#d97706" font-size="11" font-weight="800">Hemisphere</text>
									<text x="150" y="95" fill="#d97706" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Cylinder (h = L - 2r)</text>
									<text x="270" y="95" fill="#d97706" font-size="11" font-weight="800">Hemisphere</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<div class="calc-box">
								Total Volume = <strong>Volume of Cylinder + 2 × (Volume of Hemisphere)</strong><br/>
								Total Volume = <strong>πr²h + 2 × [(2/3) πr³] = πr² [h + (4/3)r]</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>A gulab jamun contains sugar syrup up to about 30% of its volume. Find how much syrup would be found in 45 gulab jamuns, each shaped like a cylinder with two hemispherical ends with length 5 cm and diameter 2.8 cm.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Diameter = 2.8 cm ⟹ Radius <em>r = 1.4 cm</em>.</p>
							<p>Height of cylinder <em>h = Total Length - 2r = 5 - 2(1.4) = 5 - 2.8 = 2.2 cm</em>.</p>

							<p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong>Step 1: Volume of 1 Gulab Jamun</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								V₁ = πr²h + (4/3)πr³ = πr² [h + (4/3)r]<br/>
								V₁ = (22/7) × 1.4 × 1.4 × [2.2 + (4/3)(1.4)]<br/>
								V₁ = 6.16 × [2.2 + 1.867] = 6.16 × 4.067 = <strong>25.05 cm³</strong>
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Step 2: Total Volume of 45 Gulab Jamuns</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								V_total = 45 × 25.05 = <strong>1127.25 cm³</strong>
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Step 3: Volume of Sugar Syrup (30%)</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Syrup Volume = 30% × 1127.25 = (30 / 100) × 1127.25 = <strong>338.18 cm³ ≈ 338 cm³</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Volume of combined solid = <strong>Direct sum of individual volumes</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Cylinder height in capsule = <strong>Total Length - 2 × radius</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Cone volume is exactly <strong>(1/3)rd</strong> of a cylinder of same radius and height.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/surface-area-of-combined-solids" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Combined Surface Area</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/applications-and-practice" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Applications & Practice</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">SURFACE AREAS & VOLUMES</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 02 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 50%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/surface-area-of-combined-solids" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Combined Surface Area</strong>
									<small>Exposed CSA sum rule</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/volume-of-combined-solids" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Combined Volume</strong>
									<small>Sum of volumes rule</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/applications-and-practice" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Applications & Practice</strong>
									<small>NCERT word problems</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

